<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47675" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχ-ήεις</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sounding, ringing, roaring</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.157
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώματα ἠχήεντα</span>
			<i>high, echoing</i> rooms or halls, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.72
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμοι ἠχήεντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					767
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1236
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰά</span> prob. l. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				915
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρόος αὐλῶν</span> Epic.
			ap. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.654f
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέττιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.196
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); of the ears, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. ἀκουή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					1.35
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέεις</span>.</div>
